go.yaml files bufio.{NewScanner,NewReader} as ipc_recv on the note "When
wrapping os.Stdin" -- a condition holding at ZERO of the 83 bare-local sites
the shipped reaching-def solver resolves across the ADR-0049 cohort, 63 of
which (74.1%) wrap an os.Open handle. ipc_recv mints untrusted_input, so those
63 invent a taint source out of a file read. This is the LARGER of the item's
two false-source populations and the one its 19.1% estimate omitted.

The analyzer runs before any DDG exists, so the origin lookup is syntactic and
deliberately smaller than the solver that measured the 83: the last binding of
the name at or above the use line, in the enclosing function only, no branch or
loop reasoning. Both ordering shapes are pinned -- a rebinding above the call
wins, a rebinding below it is not used. One classifier decides what an
expression produces, so an inline argument and a resolved binding cannot drift.

The source gate got FINER rather than gaining a sibling. The sink side asks
"does this site cross a boundary at all"; the source side needs "does it cross
one that MINTS", because a file read crosses a real boundary -- fs_read -- that
is absent from AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP by design. Conflating the two would have
meant either calling a file read "no crossing" (breaking every fs_write claim,
which counts exactly those host_path targets) or minting from it.
read_boundary_for_target_kind answers from the non-crossing set FIRST, so
widening that set at its single home still moves both arms.

Three fail-closed controls, because the direction is removal: an os.Stdin
handle reached through a local still mints; net.Dial and an http body stamp
nothing so the catalogue still decides; an unknown target kind mints. INV-vukiv
on the source side is pinned too. The superseded first-deliverable assertion is
rewritten, not deleted, and now pins what survives: a PARAMETER has no binding
to read, so the abstention stays an abstention (INV-zumin).

Measured on the 0006 cohort, both arms cold: 8 rows removed, 0 added, no
verdict moved. All eight are beads. EVERY ONE WAS READ BACK AGAINST SOURCE and
every one is `f, err := os.Open(...)` then `bufio.NewScanner(f)` -- including
one inside an if-initializer. None is a stdin, network or subprocess read. The
crossing is not lost: beads carries 55 os.Open fs_read chains, so ADR-0049
ruling 3 is satisfied by a represented crossing rather than by argument. That
is the opposite outcome to the first deliverable, whose seven removed rows each
wrapped a subprocess's stdout -- the difference is the read-back, not the delta.

Resolution rate, with the caveat that it is NOT the DDG's number: 92 of 97
wrapper call EDGES stamped (beads 65/67, cilium 15/27, jaeger 2/2, gocryptfs
1/1). Different denominator from the item's 83-of-163, which counted bare-local
textual SITES. The effect is also smaller than the stamp count suggests --
cilium resolves 15 and no finding moves, because a corrected source only
changes a verdict where it reached a sink.

Also fixes a stale meta-key declaration of my own making: io_target_kind still
listed four values after in_memory was added, and its write_discipline note
read "sole writer: bash.py" while go.py had become a second writer.

